{
  "abstract": "We study the rank-two bundles obtained by pulling the Horrocks–Mumford\nbundle back along the symmetric Kummer map from a product of four elliptic\ncurves. These bundles satisfy the weak Hochschild kernel equality\n$\\ker(\\operatorname{ev}_F)=\\operatorname{Ann}(\\operatorname{ch}(F))$. We construct their complete second-order obstruction\nfor a Poisson deformation coupled to the gerbe dictated by that equality.\nIn an explicit Thom–Whitney model, a functional with 21 integer\ncoefficients annihilates the entire boundary space, including its higher\nČech differential, and pairs with the obstruction to the constant 40.\nThe computation is over the polynomial ring in the elliptic invariants;\nthe obstruction is therefore nonzero for every nonsingular elliptic curve\nin the symmetric family. A common Dolbeault–Thom–Whitney resolution\nidentifies this obstruction with the geometric object-deformation problem.\nIt cannot be removed by changing the first object lift or the second\ncoefficient of the ambient deformation. This supplies a higher obstruction\nto categorical deformation despite the weak first-order condition. For generic independent pairs, we also prove uniform degree-two cohomology\nfor every flat twist at translation zero, and show by relative duality\nthat a globally coherent Orlov transform would necessarily be locally\nfree. The remaining condition is uniform vanishing over all translations.\nThese results do not disprove the rational Hodge conjecture or settle\nthe corresponding question for ordinary deformations of coherent sheaves.",
